# /srv/workout-explorer/.env: mode 0600, never committed (F-31 DP-6, F-59). Compose: owned by the deploy user,
# read by Compose (as the project .env) and by the app container. Podman and bare metal read only the
# WORKOUT_EXPLORER_* keys, for the app alone (RUNBOOK.md), and update.sh reads WX_UPDATE_PUBLIC_KEY.
# With notifications on it holds a secret.
# Unset or empty keys use the default shown; an invalid value stops `serve` at start (exit 2).

# Required: the site's public origin, as the operator's proxy serves it. No path, no trailing slash.
WORKOUT_EXPLORER_BASE_URL=https://workouts.example.org

# Storage cap in MB (1-1000000); keep it below free disk minus Docker's logs and one over-cap upload.
WORKOUT_EXPLORER_STORAGE_LIMIT_MB=1000
# Uploads processed at once (1-16). The memory cap in compose.yaml assumes the default 4.
WORKOUT_EXPLORER_MAX_CONCURRENT_UPLOADS=4
# Parser time limit in seconds (5-60). The runbook records the chosen value.
WORKOUT_EXPLORER_PARSE_TIMEOUT=10
# Uploads per hour: per IPv4 address, and per IPv6 /64 prefix (1-240 each).
WORKOUT_EXPLORER_UPLOADS_PER_HOUR_IPV4=60
WORKOUT_EXPLORER_UPLOADS_PER_HOUR_IPV6=60

# The operator part of the About page (who runs this site, contact, hosting, logs, legal basis): a plain text
# file you write from operator.example.txt, public to every visitor. Unset or missing: the page shows a visible
# placeholder. Read at start of `app`. Never committed. RUNBOOK.md, "The About page".
#WORKOUT_EXPLORER_OPERATOR_FILE=/srv/workout-explorer/operator/about.txt

# Optional Impressum (legal notice) at /impressum, shown after a click; footer link on every page. A plain text file
# you write from impressum.example.txt, same format as the operator file. Unset: no page, no link. Set but missing or
# invalid: `app` does not start. Read at start of `app`; published pages follow after `regenerate`. Never committed.
# RUNBOOK.md, "Impressum".
#WORKOUT_EXPLORER_IMPRESSUM_FILE=/srv/workout-explorer/operator/impressum.txt

# Report notifications through Pushover (off unless both are set; RUNBOOK.md, "Notifications").
# Both are 30 letters and digits. Also add compose.notify.yaml to COMPOSE_FILE, or app cannot reach Pushover.
#WORKOUT_EXPLORER_PUSHOVER_TOKEN=
#WORKOUT_EXPLORER_PUSHOVER_USER=

# Link to your iPhone upload Shortcut (an https:// iCloud link), shown on the About page. Unset: no section.
# RUNBOOK.md, "iPhone upload Shortcut".
#WORKOUT_EXPLORER_IOS_SHORTCUT_URL=

# Release signing key (F-52; RUNBOOK.md, "Updates"): the second line of the project's deploy/minisign.pub, after
# you compared it with the DNS TXT record. Required by update.sh, which installs every release on Docker Compose
# and rootless Podman and checks its signature with this key first. No deploy ever writes it.
#WX_UPDATE_PUBLIC_KEY=RW...
# Automatic updates (off unless "on"): a nightly timer installs every newer signed release. Also install the
# timer (DOCKER.md section 8, PODMAN.md section 9). When on, the About page says that updates come from GitHub.
#WORKOUT_EXPLORER_AUTO_UPDATE=on

# Compose only from here on.
# Host data directory (the same path is used inside the containers).
WX_DATA=/srv/workouts
# Where Caddy's plain HTTP port is published on the host. Your reverse proxy forwards here.
# Never a public address. A proxy in a container needs an address it can reach (RUNBOOK.md, "Reverse proxy").
WX_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:8088
# Addresses or CIDR prefixes (separated by spaces, not commas) whose X-Forwarded-For Caddy believes: your reverse proxy's source
# address as Caddy sees it. Unset: the Docker gateway of the edge network (10.250.0.1), which is
# right for a proxy on the host connecting to WX_LISTEN on 127.0.0.1.
#WX_TRUSTED_PROXIES=10.250.0.1

# With notifications, add the override (DOCKER.md section 5):
#COMPOSE_FILE=compose.yaml:compose.notify.yaml
# Self-builders only (DOCKER.md section 9): build the app image from a checkout.
#COMPOSE_FILE=compose.yaml:compose.build.yaml
#COMPOSE_FILE=compose.yaml:compose.build.yaml:compose.notify.yaml
